---
// Section through an ablating insulator: what is gone, what is char, what is still virgin.
---

<figure class="viz">
  <p class="viz-title">Inside an ablating wall: section, not to scale</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 820 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="cl-desc">
    <desc id="cl-desc">
      Section through motor insulation during firing. From the hot gas side: the original surface line, the eroded region
      that has been removed, a porous char layer, a thin pyrolysis zone where the rubber is decomposing, the virgin
      insulation that is still intact, the bondline, and the case. Heat flows in from the gas; pyrolysis gases flow out
      through the char. Erosion plus char is the material affected depth.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <pattern id="cl-char" width="10" height="10" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
        <rect width="10" height="10" fill="#1b1d1f"></rect>
        <circle cx="3" cy="3" r="1.6" fill="#5a5f63"></circle>
        <circle cx="8" cy="7" r="1.2" fill="#5a5f63"></circle>
      </pattern>
      <linearGradient id="cl-gas" x1="0" x2="1">
        <stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--rd-hot)" stop-opacity="0.6"></stop>
        <stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--rd-hot)" stop-opacity="0.15"></stop>
      </linearGradient>
      <marker id="cl-ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" fill="var(--rd-accent)"></path>
      </marker>
      <marker id="cl-ahb" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" fill="var(--rd-blue)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- layers, left (gas) to right (outside) -->
    <rect x="20" y="40" width="190" height="170" fill="url(#cl-gas)"></rect>
    <rect x="150" y="40" width="60" height="170" fill="none" stroke="var(--rd-muted)" stroke-dasharray="5 4"></rect>
    <rect x="210" y="40" width="130" height="170" fill="url(#cl-char)"></rect>
    <rect x="340" y="40" width="26" height="170" fill="var(--rd-propellant)" fill-opacity="0.55"></rect>
    <rect x="366" y="40" width="250" height="170" fill="var(--rd-insul)"></rect>
    <rect x="616" y="40" width="10" height="170" fill="var(--rd-warn)"></rect>
    <rect x="626" y="40" width="90" height="170" fill="var(--rd-steel)"></rect>

    <!-- labels on top -->
    <g font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--rd-ink)">
      <text x="85" y="30">hot gas</text>
      <text x="180" y="30" fill="var(--rd-muted)">eroded</text>
      <text x="275" y="30">char</text>
      <text x="353" y="30" font-size="10">pyrolysis</text>
      <text x="491" y="30">virgin insulation</text>
      <text x="621" y="30" font-size="10">bond</text>
      <text x="671" y="30">case</text>
    </g>

    <!-- flows -->
    <line x1="40" y1="90" x2="200" y2="90" stroke="var(--rd-accent)" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#cl-ah)"></line>
    <text x="50" y="80" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-accent)">heat flux in</text>
    <line x1="330" y1="150" x2="230" y2="150" stroke="#7cc7d6" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4" marker-end="url(#cl-ahb)"></line>
    <text x="232" y="172" font-size="11" fill="#e8ecef">pyrolysis gas out</text>
    <line x1="208" y1="122" x2="160" y2="122" stroke="var(--rd-ink)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cl-ah)"></line>
    <text x="60" y="140" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-ink)">surface recedes</text>
    <text x="60" y="154" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-ink)">(erosion)</text>

    <!-- dimension: material affected depth -->
    <line x1="150" y1="232" x2="366" y2="232" stroke="var(--rd-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-start="url(#cl-ah)" marker-end="url(#cl-ah)"></line>
    <text x="258" y="250" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--rd-accent)">material affected depth = erosion + char</text>
    <line x1="366" y1="268" x2="616" y2="268" stroke="var(--rd-ok)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-start="url(#cl-ah)" marker-end="url(#cl-ah)"></line>
    <text x="491" y="286" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--rd-ok)">virgin left: keeps the bondline cool</text>
    <line x1="150" y1="214" x2="150" y2="240" stroke="var(--rd-muted)"></line>
    <line x1="366" y1="214" x2="366" y2="276" stroke="var(--rd-muted)"></line>
    <line x1="616" y1="214" x2="616" y2="276" stroke="var(--rd-muted)"></line>
    <text x="150" y="226" font-size="10" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rd-muted)">original surface </text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The insulator does two jobs: it gives up its surface slowly (erosion and charring carry heat away), and the virgin
    material left behind insulates the case. Thickness must cover the affected depth with margin <em>and</em> leave
    enough virgin material to keep the bondline cool, including after burnout.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
